\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Let S be smooth connected projective complex and let $L=-K_S$ carry a smooth semipositive Hermitian metric. For any pseudo-effective Cartier divisor D, if $H^{0}(S,m_j$ $L-D)\neq 0$ for a strictly increasing sequence of positive $m_j$, must $H^{0}(S,kL)\neq 0$ for some positive k?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Let S be smooth connected projective complex and let $L=-K_S$ carry a smooth semipositive Hermitian metric. For any pseudo-effective Cartier divisor D, if $H^{0}(S,m_j$ $L-D)\neq 0$ for a strictly increasing sequence of positive $m_j$, must $H^{0}(S,kL)\neq 0$ for some positive k?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
